# NPC figures on location screens

New location screens are a flat board with 3D pieces (`tabletop-locations.mdc`). People are **separate keyed figures sitting on that board**, not painted into it, and **not** on the overworld map.

Do not generate isometric walkers. Do not put people on hex terrain bases (those bases are for buildings).

The live game still shows Tomas-bevel standees (`assets/npcs/tomas_standee_bevel_v19.png` and the matching Nessa/Bram/Elira/Beph cutouts). Leave those in `index.html` until the location rebuild. If a new location mock needs a person before Marc picks a new construction, reuse those oak cutouts on the board.

If Marc explicitly asks to patch the **current** live streets before the rebuild, keep the old oak construction:

- Painted figure on a chunky routed oak board
- Wood-grain bevel, rectangular stained-wood foot
- One ALL-CAPS plaque (TOMAS, NESSA, BRAM, ELIRA, BEPH)
- Lime `#00FF00` chroma for cutouts
- Four standing anchors per location; `syncTownStandees()` only; no extra observers
